<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n8399" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀνεπί-ληπτος</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ον</span>,
			<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>not open to attack,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τοῖς ἐχθροῖς</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Th.
					5.17
				</span></i>
			; <i>not censured, blameless,</i>
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">βίος</span>
			v.l. in
			<i><span class="en">
				E.
				<u>Or.</u>
				922
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				X.
				<u>Cyr.</u>
				1.2.15
			</span></i>; <i>perfect,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τέχνη</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Ph.
					1.15
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀνεπιληπτότερον</span>”
				<i>less open to criticism,</i>
				 <i><span class="en">
					Pl.
					<u>Phlb.</u>
					43c
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐξουσία ἀ.</span>”
				<i>not subject to control,</i>
				 <i><span class="en">
					D.H.
					2.14
				</span></i>
			; <i>unassailable, not subject to cancellation,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">συγγραφαί</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					<u>PTaur.</u>
					1.7.15
				</span></i>
			. Adv.
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">-τως</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					X.
					<u>An.</u>
					7.6.37
				</span></i>
			, <i><span class="en">
				Ph.
				2.2
			</span></i>,al.</div>
